<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-UAL Corp estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-UAL Corp estimates raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Gruntal &amp; Co on Thursday said it raised its 1997 earnings estimate for UAL Corp, the parent of United Airlines, to $9.50 a share from $8.50 and reiterated its outperform (speculative) rating.</p>
<p>-- Gruntal also raised its estimate for UAL's first-quarter earnings to $1.40 a share from $1.00.</p>
<p>-- Gruntal said United had the best load factor in the industry in February (68.4 percent) on double-digit traffic and capacity increases.</p>
<p>-- UAL shares closed down 5/8 at 67-3/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
